een elevated in the morning.\n\nPHYSICAL EXAM\n\nEYES\n- PERRLA, extra-ocular motility, pupils equal and reactive to light and accommodation. No conjunctival injection or erythema.\n\nEARS\n- Normal ear canals and tympanic membranes. No discharge or erythema.\n\nNECK\n- Supple with no cyanosis or bruising. No thyromegaly.\n\nRESPIRATORY\n- Lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally. No wheezing, rales, or rhonchi.\n\nCARDIOVASCULAR\n- Regular rate and rhythm. No murmurs, gallops, or rubs.\n\nGI/GU\n- Gastrointestinal: No tenderness to palpation. No hepatosplenomegaly.\n\nMSK\n- Examination of the low back: Pain with palpation of the mid and lower back. Positive Patrick\'s and Gaenslen\'s signs on the left side.\n\nRESULTS\n\nX-rays of the lumbar spine are ordered.\n\nASSESSMENT AND PLAN\n\n1. Low back strain.\n- Medical Reasoning: The patient is complaining of low back pain for the past week. He has tried taking over the counter medications for pain relief with no improvement. He has a history of diabetes and is compliant with his medications. He is overweight. He reports that his low back pain is constant and he experiences pain when he makes sudden movements to the left. He has pain when he walks. He has pain with palpation of the mid and lower back on the left side. He has positive Patrick\'s and Gaenslen\'s signs on the left side. He denies any numbness or tingling in his feet.\n- Patient Education and Counseling: I advised the patient of the nature of his diagnosis and the plan for management. I advised him that we will order an x-ray of the lumbar spine to rule out any bony abnormalities. I advised him that if the x-ray shows any abnormalities, we will order a CT scan of the lumbar spine. I advised him to avoid any strenuous activity and to follow up with me after the x-ray results.\n- Medical Treatment: I have prescribed Flexeril 10mg tablets one tablet daily for pain and inflammation. I have also prescribed ibuprofen 400mg tablets to be taken as needed for 